    "Counting rules: lowercase fold; split on whitespace (em/en-dash split too); surrounding punctuation stripped; apostrophes kept mid-word, stripped at the edges; hyphenated words are single forms; a form counts only if it contains a letter.",
    "Excluded 24 non-letter forms (numbers, ranges, dates, lone punctuation — not words for the idea-2 constraint): -, 1, 1.5.14, 136-78, 144, 154-156, 158, 167, 17, 2, 200, 241, 264, 3, 300, 323, 37, 38-39, 400, 600-500, 700, ·, •, →",
    "10 confirmed forms carry the transcription's own [[struck / ]] markup fragments and are kept exactly as they appear (no silent cleanup): child[[ins, gently[[struck, l]]legs, like]][[struck, memories[[struck, my]]self, possibilit[[struck, simple[[struck, un]]finished, your]][[struck",
    "16 confirmed forms carry an internal / or # (alternative readings such as d/c, carefully/carelessly) and are kept exactly as they appear.",
    "Uncertain words are the single-quoted candidate readings in the 312 per-page u notes (669 quoted spans); 9 notes hold no quoted span and contribute nothing.",
    "Ideas 2 and 4 (new poems limited to journal vocabulary; poem 100 from poems 1-99) and whether machine-misread readings count under the no-AI-text rule remain the author's call; this file reports both counts instead of choosing."
